		<FeatureExplanations>
			<string>[HL]Leader Changes:[/HL] note that [B]Atuuks do not follow the normal leader change mechanisms of their chosen government[/B]. Instead they select new leaders using the [B]Great Direction[/B] and [B]Great One[/B] features outlined below. Thus Atuuk factions cannot manually dismiss their Leader</string>
			<string>[HL]The Great Direction:[/HL] every 5 years select from a choice of three Great Directions with associated bonuses which apply for 5 years. There are seven Great Directions in all, each with a unique victory objective</string>
			<string>[HL]Who is Great?:[/HL] periodically presented with a choice of two characters to be designated Great Atuuks of the future. Whichever one is chosen gains the [B]Great Potential[/B] trait, making them eligible for future leadership</string>
			<string>[HL]The Great One:[/HL] whenever the Great Direction changes, there is a 25% chance that a new Faction Leader must then be chosen from two randomly-selected characters with the [B]Great Potential[/B] trait. The new leader may turn out to have the right qualities to be [B]The Great One[/B]. Alternatively, the new leader may turn out to be a disappointment ([B]Not The Great One[/B]), leading to a reselection one year later</string>
			<string>[HL]Direction Doubt:[/HL] whenever the Great Direction changes, there is a 20% chance that some Atuuk have doubts about the change. If so, then for two years the Atuuk suffer -10% Happiness as they adjust to the new direction</string>
			<string>[HL]Rapid Unscheduled Disassembly:[/HL] occasionally an Atuuk state ship will suffer a major failure due to poor engineering. The ship will likely experience major damage, or it may even be completely destroyed. More likely to happen to ships in hyperspace.</string>
			<string>[HL]What Does This Button Do?:[/HL] whenever a Critical Research Success occurs there is a choice to Push the Button or Don't Push the Button, leading to various positive or negative events</string>
			<string>[HL]Deadly... in Numbers:[/HL] +25% ground combat bonus when Atuuk troop units outnumber their enemy during a colony battle</string>
			<string>[HL]We Are Great!:[/HL] +5% Happiness and +10% Corruption Reduction for one year whenever sign a Free Trade Agreement, Research Treaty or Defense Treaty</string>
			<string>[HL]Unique Leader trait - Prosperous:[/HL] +5% Colony Income, +5% Trade Income</string>
			<string>[HL]Unique Leader trait - First of Many:[/HL] +5% Colony Population Growth</string>
			<string>[HL]Unique Leader trait - The Great One:[/HL] +10% Empire Happiness</string>
			<string>[HL]Unique Leader trait - Not The Great One:[/HL] -20% Empire Happiness</string>
			<string>[HL]Unique Ambassador trait - Endearing:[/HL] +5% Diplomacy, +10% PsyOps</string>
			<string>[HL]Unique Ambassador trait - Gullible:[/HL] -5% Diplomacy, -10% Trade Income</string>
			<string>[HL]Unique General trait - Honored Hunter:[/HL] +10% Troop Attack Strength</string>
			<string>[HL]Unique Admiral trait - Speed Maniac:[/HL] +20% Ship Speed, +20% Ship Maneuvering, -10% Ship Maintenance Savings</string>
			<string>[HL]Unique Scientist trait - Intuitive:[/HL] +10% Construction Research</string>
			<string>[HL]Unique Spy trait - Cute But Deadly:[/HL] +10% Espionage, +10% Assassination</string>
